.         
.         * OUTCOME VARIABLE
.         * The outcome variable measuring support for gender equality is an ag
> gregated index constructed from three survey items: plj0625, plj0624, and plj
> 0622
.         * Each is measured on a 1-7 likert scale and contributes equally to t
> he index 'support_gender_equality.'
.         gen support_gender_equality = (plj0625 + plj0624 + plj0622 - 3) /18
(3,721 missing values generated)

.         keep if support_gender_equality!=.
(3,721 observations deleted)

.         
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1
.         * Our model is a linear regression (OLS) estimating how having a daug
> hter relates to support for gender equality, controling for age and age squar
> ed, as well as number of daughters and number of sons. Standard errors are cl
> ustered at the household level.
.         * Remark: The survey items (plj0625, plj0624, and plj0622) used to co
> nstruct the outcome variable are available for only a single year per respond
> ent, not across three years as initially assumed. Therefore, we could not imp
> lement the panel regression specified in the PAP and instead used an OLS mode
> l. The variables and controls remain consistent with those outlined in the PA
> P.
.         reg support_gender_equality has_daughter has_child age age2 numberson
> s numberdaughters, cluster(cid)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        250
                                                F(6, 162)         =       2.08
